 ## Background
-Trilinear interpolation is a standard technique in computer graphics for dense grids [S3, unofficial]. Trilinear Gradient Interpolation extends this to vector fields. The method is commonly used in volume rendering for cloud shading [S1, unofficial] and in implicit surface rendering for normal estimation [S3, unofficial]. The specific implementation for normals is detailed in the SDFDiff project [S3, unofficial].
